{"translation-revision-date":"2023-09-21 21:49+0000","generator":"WP-CLI\/2.12.0","source":"assets\/js\/admin\/features\/cron-jobs.js","domain":"messages","locale_data":{"messages":{"":{"domain":"messages","lang":"de-DE","plural-forms":"nplurals=2; plural=n != 1;"},"Something went wrong...":["Etwas ist schiefgegangen..."],"Upload it to the root directory of WordPress. This is the same folder as your <code>wp-config.php<\/code> file.":["Lade sie ins Stammverzeichnis von WordPress hoch. Das ist der gleiche Ordner wie deine Datei <code>wp-config.php<\/code>."],"Copied to clipboard!":[""],"Setup using Cron-Job.org":[""],"Cron-Job.org is a free service that we trust to keep your site running smoothly.":[""],"Create an account on <a href=\"https:\/\/cron-job.org\">Cron-Job.org<\/a>.":[""],"Once logged in, click <b>CREATE CRONJOB<\/b>.":[""],"Copy the following into the <b>URL<\/b> field.":[""],"Set the <b>Execution Schedule<\/b> to \"Every <b>1<\/b> minutes(s)\".":[""],"Finish by clicking <b>CREATE<\/b>.":[""],"Setup using CPanel":[""],"Many hosts use CPanel for backend hosting administration. If your server uses CPanel you can use its built-in Cron Jobs tool.":[""],"Once logged into your CPanel open the Cron Jobs tool.":[""],"Under <b>Add New Cron Job<\/b> select <code>Once Per Minute(*****)<\/code> from the <b>Common Settings<\/b> dropdown.":[""],"Copy the following into the <b>Command<\/b> field.":[""],"Replace <code>\/path\/to\/public_html\/<\/code> with the real file location.":[""],"Finish by clicking <b>Add New Cron Job<\/b>.":[""],"Setup using SiteGround":[""],"SiteGround provides their own proprietary Cron Job tool which you should use for best results. If you have difficulties please open a ticket with SiteGround for assistance.":[""],"Login to your <a href=\"https:\/\/login.siteground.com\/login\">SiteGround account<\/a> and click on <b>Site Tools<\/b> for the site where %s is installed.":[""],"Click <b>DEVS<\/b> in the left-hand menu, then <b>Cron Jobs<\/b> in the expanded menu.":[""],"Under <b>Create New Cron Job<\/b>, copy the following into the <b>Command<\/b> field.":[""],"Confirm the file location %s is correct.":[""],"Enter %s into the <b>Interval<\/b> field.":[""],"Finish by clicking <b>Create<\/b>.":[""],"Setup using Cloudways":[""],"Cloudways provides their own proprietary Cron Job tool which you should use for best results. If you have difficulties please open a ticket with Cloudways for assistance.":[""],"Login to your <a href=\"https:\/\/login.siteground.com\/login\">Cloudways account<\/a> and navigate to <b>Applications<\/b>.":[""],"Open the application that has %s installed, then click <b>Cron Job Management<\/b> in the left-hand menu.":[""],"Click on the <b>Advanced<\/b> tab, then click the <b>ADD NEW CRON JOB<\/b> button.":[""],"Then select <code>Every minute(* * * * *)<\/code> from the <b>Common Settings<\/b> dropdown.":[""],"Enter %s into the <b>Command<\/b> field.":[""],"Finish by clicking <b>SUBMIT<\/b>.":[""],"Setup using Kinsta":[""],"Kinsta does not provide a dedicated UI to manage cron jobs. Instead, you must ask Kinsta support to add them for you, or follow <a href=\"https:\/\/kinsta.com\/docs\/wordpress-hosting\/site-management\/cron-jobs\/\">Kinsta's guide on adding cron jobs via the command line<\/a>.":[""],"If you are asking Kinsta support for help, ask them to \"Create a PHP cron job to run the %s file in the WordPress root directory every minute.\"":[""],"Generic setup instructions":[""],"For any other method, you essentially want a script to call the URL below <b>once every minute<\/b>.":[""],"\u26a0\ufe0f The %1$s cron is not running on time and was last run %2$s":[""],"The %1$s cron is running on time and was last run %2$s.":[""],"Do cron jobs give you <i>anxiety<\/i>?":[""],"Let our team help you set them up correctly! First time customers can have our team install Groundhogg, import contacts, connect SMTP, and set up cron jobs!":[""],"MORE DETAILS &rarr;":[""],"Disable the WordPress Internal Cron":[""],"The internal WordPress cron system sends an asynchronous request to the <code>wp-cron.php<\/code> on every page load. This can slow down your site and create a poor experience for site visitors. We recommend disabling it. You will replace it with an external cron job which is much faster and better for performance.":[""],"Internal cron disabled!":[""],"The WordPress internal cron is disabled":[""],"Disable the internal WordPress Cron":[""],"Install the %s Cron File":[""],"We recommend installing a special file in the root directory of your site that will create a separate cron system for %s. This will be more reliable than the core WordPress cron system for handling important automation and scheduled emails.":[""],"Cron file installed!":[""],"Cron file not installed. Please install it manually.":[""],"The file has been installed":[""],"Install the special cron file":[""],"Install the cron file manually":[""],"If automatic installation of the cron file does not work follow these steps.":[""],"Download the cron file.":[""],"Change the file extension from <code>.txt<\/code> to <code>.php<\/code> so that it appears as <code>gh-cron.php<\/code>.":[""],"Configuring Core WordPress Cron":[""],"The core WordPress cron is responsible for %s background tasks (importing contacts, scheduling broadcasts), as well as WordPress background tasks (publishing scheduled posts, auto updating plugins).":[""],"\u26a0\ufe0f The core WordPress cron is not running on time and was last run %s":[""],"The core WordPress cron is running on time and was last run %s.":[""],"We recommend that the core WordPress cron be run <b>once every minute<\/b> for the best performance. The <i>minimum<\/i> recommendation is every 15 minutes.":[""],"Configuring %s Cron":[""],"The %s cron is responsible for sending scheduled emails and doing flow automation.":[""],"We recommend it be set to run <b>once every minute<\/b> for the best performance. The <i>minimum<\/i> recommendation is every 5 minutes.":[""]}}}